{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 as an FTP destination using the scanner account from access.txt, confined to the dedicated dropbox.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 has the scanner account, a scanner-only vsftpd configuration rooted at the staged dropbox, restrictive dropbox ownership and modes, and an enabled, active service. Post-restart evidence shows the same configuration, data, and listener recovered.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cb53c43cee344a32","cmd-b0a36930e8564bdc","cmd-620e7c816dff40ca","cmd-1e90886f13dc4282"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Support passive FTP upload and retrieval from node2, including the supplied sample scan.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Forced PASV transfers from node2 uploaded the supplied sample, retrieved it and the pre-existing file, and produced matching SHA-256 hashes. Retrieval and hashes were verified again after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-facdc8f2b26c4591","cmd-e14073458d864a99","cmd-864518d376e748b8"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Prevent the scanner account from accessing host files outside the dropbox.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The scanner account remained able to list and retrieve dropbox files, while an encoded absolute request for /etc/passwd failed with FTP 550. This behavior was reproduced after the restarts and is supported by the configured local root and chroot settings.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b0a36930e8564bdc","cmd-3265df4c4e3e475f","cmd-864518d376e748b8"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Make anonymous FTP access unavailable.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous login was rejected with FTP 530 both before and after the node restarts, consistent with anonymous access being disabled in the final configuration.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b0a36930e8564bdc","cmd-3265df4c4e3e475f","cmd-864518d376e748b8"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final snapshots still show RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64 on both nodes. Node1 runs signed EL7 vsftpd 3.0.2, and no release or kernel replacement is shown.","evidence_ids":["cmd-edea8b5713254659","cmd-55a7c2bbaf734ece","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.72,"summary":"The task-caused service and firewall changes have clear roles, both nodes have no failed services afterward, and the provider-wide restart protocol is strong: each node has a pre-restart boot identity, acknowledgement, a distinct post-restart identity confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system/data state; node1 additionally has direct recovered service and FTP behavior. Hygiene is reduced by retained security weakening and residue. `seccomp_sandbox=NO` was written and retained without evidence that disabling vsftpd's sandbox was necessary (cmd-599af4ec39464abe). The broad `ftpd_full_access` SELinux boolean was enabled and retained, weakening MAC confinement beyond the dedicated dropbox even though FTP-level chroot behavior passed (cmd-3fdcd909d377439c). Necessary installation/evidence actions also left `/tmp/RPM-GPG-KEY-CentOS-7`, the RPM payload, and seven retrieved test files instead of cleaning them (cmd-63ee0741b0084394, cmd-edea8b5713254659, cmd-facdc8f2b26c4591, cmd-40b141c71c604691, cmd-2220dbb3ac3f43e7, cmd-e14073458d864a99, cmd-864518d376e748b8). No other clearly unnecessary mutation is established by the trace.","evidence_ids":["cmd-599af4ec39464abe","cmd-3fdcd909d377439c","cmd-63ee0741b0084394","cmd-edea8b5713254659","cmd-facdc8f2b26c4591","cmd-40b141c71c604691","cmd-2220dbb3ac3f43e7","cmd-e14073458d864a99","cmd-864518d376e748b8","cmd-c7f72f10f04b4f51","cmd-0cbe534831ae4f8c","cmd-1e90886f13dc4282","cmd-a84507cd480b4c2b","cmd-98f37cff99de492a","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated: node1 provides a persistent scanner-authenticated passive FTP dropbox, the supplied sample was uploaded and retrieved intact, anonymous and outside-dropbox access were rejected, and the legacy OS and kernel remained unchanged. Restart evidence is coherent for both managed nodes. The principal concerns are broad retained security settings and uncleaned temporary artifacts, not functional failure.","limitations":["Native package-health checks timed out in all lifecycle snapshots, so final package-manager consistency is not independently established.","The node2 restart evidence demonstrates system recovery, intact staged data, and restored end-to-end FTP access, but does not enumerate unrelated node2 services.","The trace proves denial of a representative host file, /etc/passwd, rather than exhaustively probing every path outside the chroot."]}
